      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ios): unify chat and voice experience",
        "body": "Closes #107804\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\niOS split conversational input across Chat and a separate Talk destination. Moving between typing, dictation, attachments, voice notes, and realtime voice therefore felt like changing modes, while connection, tool, and voice activity could outlive the chat session that started it.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis makes Chat the single conversational destination. One composer mic handles tap-to-dictate and long-press/menu **Record Voice Note**, while realtime Talk remains a chat action backed by the existing runtime. The separate Talk tab and its obsolete UI state are removed; shipped `talk` / `voice` launch aliases now route to Chat.\n\nThe same ownership model now covers dictation, Photo Library, file import, camera encoding, voice-note staging, and Live Activity updates. Each asynchronous path captures its originating view model plus full session/routing snapshot, rejects stale completion, and balances audio/attachment ownership. One Live Activity arbiter prioritizes attention, tools, voice, connection, and hydrated fallback state for the avatar and Dynamic Island.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Chat, dictation, voice notes, attachments, and realtime voice live in one surface with one microphone affordance.\n- Voice memo is preserved: tap the mic for dictation; long-press or use its menu to record a voice note; the composer switches to the recording row while capture is active.\n- The agent avatar carries compact connection status and ambient audio feedback; the Dynamic Island shows system-native voice/tool/attention activity without drawing a fake or split island around the camera cutout.\n- Switching sessions, agents, gateways, or routing while async work is suspended cannot publish text, media, errors, or activity into the new owner.\n\nNew locale source entries intentionally remain source-equal in generated artifacts; `.github/workflows/native-app-locale-refresh.yml` owns post-merge translation refresh.\n\nAI assistance was used for implementation and review. The behavior and proof were manually directed and verified.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unified Chat composer\n\n<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/unified-chat.png\" alt=\"Unified Chat composer with attachment, dictation, realtime voice, and four-tab navigation\" width=\"360\">\n\n### Attachment menu\n\n![Attachment menu opening from the unified composer](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/attachment-menu.gif)\n\n### Voice-note menu and live recording waveform\n\n![Long-press voice-note menu transitioning into the live recording row](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/voice-note-flow.gif)\n\n### Real Gateway avatar status and audio activity\n\n![Real Gateway avatar status expanding from its compact dot](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/avatar-status.gif)\n\n![Real Gateway avatar showing ambient audio activity](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/avatar-audio.gif)\n\n### Dynamic Island voice activity\n\n![Dynamic Island showing the real Gateway avatar and live voice waveform](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/dynamic-island.gif)\n\nFull-resolution stills: [attachment menu](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/attachment-menu.png), [voice-note recording](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/voice-note-recording.png), [avatar status](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/avatar-status.png), [avatar audio](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/avatar-audio.png), and [Dynamic Island](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac/openclaw/pr-107879/v2/dynamic-island.png).\n\nVisual proof is stored outside the OpenClaw source branch in [Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets@00c2222](https://github.com/Solvely-Colin/pr-proof-assets/commit/00c22222adfa46852511e56713c4b33e291238ac). The sequence paired fresh to the real LAN Gateway and passed end to end on the iOS 26.2 simulator; no screenshot/demo fixture was used.\n\n- Physical iPhone + real Gateway QA: unified composer, voice note, realtime voice, avatar waveform/status, and Dynamic Island behavior exercised successfully.\n- iPhone 17 Pro simulator (`OpenClaw Island QA`, iOS 26.2): 289/289 focused iOS tests passed, including Live Activity arbitration, app-model invoke/audio ownership, Talk config, and root-tab presentation.\n- Shared Swift routing/ownership suite: 8/8 passed; unified mic contract tests: 2/2 passed.\n- Full `VoiceNoteRecorderTests`: 14/14 passed.\n- UI test target `build-for-testing`: succeeded.\n- Native locale inventory: 4,570 entries, no drift; Apple i18n check passed (`iosKeys=1390`, 21 locales).\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Structured autoreview completed. Accepted picker-ownership findings were fixed across Photo Library, file import, and camera; remaining partitioned findings were rejected with full-path cancellation/session proof and successful macOS compilation.\n",
        "branch": "ios-unified-chat-voice",
